SECURITY POLICY FOR WHY2
========================

1. REPORTING A VULNERABILITY
----------------------------
We take the security of WHY2 seriously. If you discover a security vulnerability,
please bring it to our attention strictly via email.

DO NOT report security vulnerabilities through public GitHub/GitLab issues.

Please send a detailed description of the vulnerability to the project maintainer:

    Email: engo@satan.red

We will acknowledge receipt of your vulnerability report within 48 hours and
strive to send you regular updates about our progress.

2. SECURITY ARCHITECTURE & FEATURES
-----------------------------------
WHY2 is designed with a "defense-in-depth" approach, leveraging modern Rust
features and cryptographic best practices where possible. However, it relies on
a custom cryptographic primitive.

A) Cryptographic Primitives
   - Algorithm: WHY2 (REX) is a symmetric block cipher based on a configurable
     Grid (matrix) of 64-bit cells.
   - Design Principle: ARX (Add-Rotate-XOR) network for nonlinear mixing.
     No S-boxes are used, eliminating cache-timing attacks related to memory lookups.
   - Mode of Operation: CTR (Counter) mode is used for encryption.
   - Randomness: Uses ChaCha20Rng (via `rand` crate) for CSPRNG requirements.

B) Implementation Security
   - Memory Safety: Written in pure Rust to prevent buffer overflows and
     memory-related vulnerabilities.
   - Secure Erasure: Implements the `zeroize` trait to scrub sensitive data
     (keys, plaintexts, grids) from memory immediately after use.
   - Constant-Time Execution: The core mixing functions (subcell, shift_rows)
     implement constant-time logic when the `constant-time` feature is enabled.

C) Integrity & Authenticity
   - Encrypt-then-MAC: The `auth` module implements a standard Encrypt-then-MAC scheme.
   - Algorithm: Uses HMAC-SHA256 to guarantee data integrity and authenticity.
   - Verification: MAC verification is performed in constant time before any
     decryption takes place.

3. SECURITY LIMITATIONS & RISK ASSESSMENT
-----------------------------------------
Users must be aware of the following limitations. WHY2 is experimental software.

A) No Formal Audit
   WHY2 has NOT undergone a formal external security audit by a professional
   cryptographer. There may be undiscovered weaknesses in the algorithm design
   or implementation.

B) Custom Cryptography
   WHY2 is NOT a NIST-standardized algorithm. It should not be used in environments
   requiring FIPS compliance or high-assurance security (e.g., banking, medical data).

C) Side-Channel Resistance
   While we use constant-time coding practices, WHY2 does not have hardware-level
   protection (unlike AES-NI). Power analysis or sophisticated electromagnetic
   side-channel attacks may still be possible on physical access.

